.TH "ROARK\-CONNECTIONS\-CALENDAR\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-connections-calendar-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-connections\-calendar\-create \- Connect a calendar account
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark connections calendar create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Verifies the credential against the provider and, only if it works, stores it encrypted. A credential the provider rejects is a 400 and no connection is created: a connection that has never worked would next be exercised by an inbound call at 2am, with nobody there to fix it.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/connections/calendar
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-provider\fR \fI<value>\fR
Who holds the calendar. CAL_COM and GO_HIGH_LEVEL are connected with a key, GO_HIGH_LEVEL also needing the sub\-account the key belongs to; GOOGLE and CALENDLY are connected by consent, through `POST /v1/connections/calendar/google/authorize\-url` and `POST /v1/connections/calendar/calendly/authorize\-url`. One of: CAL_COM, GOOGLE, CALENDLY, GO_HIGH_LEVEL. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<value>\fR
Customer\-facing name for this account, unique within the project. Required. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\fR \fI<value>\fR
The provider account’s API key. For CAL_COM, a Cal.com API key (starts with `cal_`). For GO_HIGH_LEVEL, a sub\-account Private Integration Token, which must carry the `calendars.readonly`, `calendars/events.readonly`, `calendars/events.write`, `contacts.readonly`, `contacts.write` and `locations.readonly` scopes. It is verified against the provider before anything is stored, so an invalid key is a 400 and no connection is created. Stored encrypted and never returned. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-go\-high\-level\-location\fR \fI<value>\fR
Required for GO_HIGH_LEVEL and ignored by every other provider: the sub\-account the token belongs to, for example `ve9EPM428h8vShlRW1KT`. A Private Integration Token does not name its own sub\-account and every calendar call needs one, so the two are stored and verified together: a token minted in a different sub\-account is a 400. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-timezone\fR \fI<value>\fR
The named IANA timezone to offer slots in, for example `America/Los_Angeles`. Omit to adopt the provider account’s own timezone. A fixed offset such as `\-08:00` is rejected: it does not observe DST. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark connections calendar create \-\-provider <value> \-\-label <value> \-\-api\-key <value>
.fi
.RE
